  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Write once, send later",
      "items": [
        "the entity and the outbox row commit in the same Room transaction — a crash cannot lose the intent to send",
        "the row carries an idempotency key, so a retry after a crash cannot apply the change twice",
        "a fire-and-forget mutation with no idempotency key and no rollback is a review finding, not a style preference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The worker drains",
      "items": [
        "WorkManager is for deferrable guaranteed work: constraints, backoff and a dead-letter view",
        "the worker reads the pending rows, posts them and settles each row — the server is authoritative for game state, prices and entitlements",
        "WorkManagerTestInitHelper is how the idempotency and the retry are proven, alongside an in-memory Room database"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What the user sees",
      "items": [
        "a 409 conflict is resolved by the server: the local pending change is rejected visibly, never silently dropped",
        "the Room Flow is the single source of truth for the screen — a sealed UiState renders loading, empty, error, forbidden, offline and ready",
        "clear user data on sign-out or tenant switch, pending outbox rows included"
      ]
    }
  ]
